  "articleBody": "Swapping out an old vanity sounds straightforward until you realize how quickly plumbing alignments, wall studs, and floor levels can complicate things. If you are preparing to hire someone for your bathroom upgrade, a few quick checks will protect your budget and prevent costly rework down the road.\n\nWhat to Prepare Before You Start:\nFirst, measure your rough-in plumbing height and width against the vanity cabinet you want. Many stock cabinets have fixed interior shelves or drawers that collide directly with your existing drain trap or shutoff valves. Second, check whether your floor extends completely beneath the old footprint; older bathrooms often have unfinished subfloor or missing tile under original cabinets. Third, check if your walls are square and plumb. An uneven wall creates noticeable gaps along the sides of a flat-back vanity cabinet.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps:\nIf your new vanity requires shifting supply lines, moving the drain pipe inside the wall, or repairing damaged subfloors, hiring an experienced general contractor saves you major headaches. HH Remodeling LLC handles full-scope bathroom updates across Denver, Aurora, and nearby communities, coordinating plumbing needs alongside finish carpentry and drywall repairs. Call Abraham Becerra at 303-505-0866 to discuss your bathroom vanity installation.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
